# P6 implementation standards

**Rule:** Guest portal and public marketing must follow the **same trunk stack** as Denali operator admin — not a one-off UI or ad-hoc fetch layer.

**Theming authority:** [`p6-enterprise-theming-architecture.mdoc`](p6-enterprise-theming-architecture.mdoc) — four-layer cascade (primitives → shell-bridge → tenant runtime → workspace skin).

Reference implementation: **`apps/web`** `(app)/` + `auth/login` + `/tours/new` wizard bridge.

---

## 1. Layer cake (do not invert)

```text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ apps/{web|portal|marketing}  — thin routes + BFF only   │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ packages/workspaces/denali — product rules, HTTP, UI    │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ apps/api — identity, tenant, canonical, workspace routes  │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ packages/workspace-sdk · tenant-kernel · platform-events │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

| Layer | Allowed in P6 | Forbidden |
| ----- | ------------- | --------- |
| `apps/*` | Layout, shell, BFF `app/api/*`, `src/features/*` logic | Business rules copied from legacy; direct DB |
| `packages/workspaces/denali` | Registration HTTP, catalog card, finance hooks | Import from `apps/*` |
| `packages/platform-core` | — | **No** P6 product diff (INV-P9-001 carryover) |

---

## 2. Design stack (Phase 2 covenant — same as admin)

Locked order — identical to [`ADMIN-SHELL-UX.md`](../phase-9/appendices/ADMIN-SHELL-UX.md) §1:

| # | Package | Admin (`apps/web`) | Portal / Marketing (P6) |
| - | ------- | ------------------ | ----------------------- |
| 1 | `@app-tour/design-tokens` | `styles.css` + inline bridge (or `shell-bridge.css`) | **`guest-shell.css`** = `index.css` + **`shell-bridge.css`** |
| 2 | Tailwind v4 | `@import "tailwindcss"` once in `globals.css` | Same — **no rules in globals** |
| 3 | `@app-tour/theme-react` | `ThemeProviderChain` (operator + plugin) | `PlatformThemeProvider` + `TenantThemeProvider` |
| 4 | Workspace skin | `workspace-theme-stylesheets.generated` | **`workspace-guest-theme-stylesheets.generated`** |
| 5 | `@app-tour/ui-primitives` | **Subpath only** | Same |
| 6 | `next-intl` | `messages/{fa,en}/*.json` | Same |

### Primitives (mandatory)

```typescript
// ✅ OK
import { Input } from "@app-tour/ui-primitives/input";
import { Button } from "@app-tour/ui-primitives/button";

// ❌ FAIL — P3-E-BARREL · eslint in apps/web
import { Input } from "@app-tour/ui-primitives";
```

### Styling rules

- **No hex in TSX** for semantic colors — use CSS vars (`var(--primary)`, `bg-primary`, token semantics).
- **No raw `<input>`** in forms — `ui-primitives/input` or `LocalizedNumericInput` (see `apps/web/scripts/guard-no-raw-wizard-input.mjs`).
- **Tenant primary** flows from `TenantThemeProvider` / branding API — not hard-coded `#0f766e` in components.
- **RTL:** `dir` on `<html>` from locale; Persian digits via `format-localized-digits` (admin + portal already do this).

### Workspace skin (Denali only)

| App | Skin file | Scope |
| --- | --------- | ----- |
| Admin | `denali-admin.css` | `body[data-workspace-plugin="denali"]` |
| Portal | `denali-portal.css` | `body[data-app-surface="portal"][data-workspace-plugin="denali"]` |
| Marketing | `denali-marketing.css` | `body[data-app-surface="marketing"][data-workspace-plugin="denali"]` |

Manifest: `guestThemeStylesheets.portal` / `.marketing` → generated bootstrap imports.

Operator chrome patterns (`PageHeader`, `DenaliEmptyState`) live in **`apps/web/src/admin/patterns/`** — **do not copy** into portal; use primitives + minimal guest layout.

---

## 3. App architecture pattern (copy from admin)

### 3.1 Thin route · fat feature

```text
app/.../page.tsx          ← server: bootstrap, fetch, pass props
app/.../*-client.tsx      ← client: compose UI
src/features/<domain>/    ← *-logic.ts (pure) · *-types.ts · copy in messages
```

Admin examples:

- `apps/web/src/features/bookings/bookings-command-center-logic.ts`
- `apps/web/src/features/auth/operator-login-logic.ts`
- `apps/web/app/auth/login/login-form.tsx`

Portal P6-1 target refactor (when touching OTP):

```text
src/features/auth/public-registration-logic.ts   ← step machine helpers
src/features/auth/public-registration-types.ts
app/catalog/.../public-catalog-registration-flow.tsx  ← thin compose
```

### 3.2 BFF-only browser → API

```text
Browser  →  /api/public-auth/*  →  apps/api /public/auth/*
Browser  →  /api/catalog/registrations  →  workspace HTTP
```

**Never** call `TOUR_OPS_API_URL` from client components. Same pattern as admin `(app)/` BFF routes.

Headers: `x-tenant-id` from host bootstrap (`buildIdentityBffHeadersAsync` / `resolvePortalBootstrapForHost`).

### 3.3 Test hooks (`data-*`)

Stable selectors for Playwright — same discipline as admin:

| Flow | Markers |
| ---- | ------- |
| OTP register | `data-public-registration-phone`, `-otp`, `-profile`, `-intake`, `-success` |
| Operator login | `OPERATOR_LOGIN_TEST_IDS` in `operator-login-copy.ts` |

Do not use CSS class names as sole E2E selectors.

---

## 4. Auth OTP (shared contract — admin vs guest)

Same API spine; different apps and post-login path:

| | Operator admin | Guest portal (P6-1) |
| --- | ---------------- | ------------------- |
| App | `apps/web` `:3000` | `apps/portal` `:3003` |
| UI | `auth/login/login-form.tsx` | `src/catalog/public-catalog-registration-flow.tsx` |
| BFF | `/api/auth/*` (owner session) | `/api/public-auth/*` |
| API | `/auth/*` | `/public/auth/*` |
| Dev OTP | `1234` (`otp.service.ts`) | **Same** |
| After OTP | Dashboard `(app)/` | New → profile (name*) → tour intake |

**Do not fork OTP verify logic** — shared package export:

```typescript
import {
  normalizeOtpDigits,
  OTP_SEGMENT_LENGTH,
} from "@app-tour/ui-primitives/otp-segment-input-logic";
```

Apps (`apps/web`, `apps/portal`) keep thin `otp-segment-input.tsx` UI shells; logic lives in `packages/ui-primitives/src/utils/otp-segment-input.logic.ts`. Allowed subpath: `import-boundary-ast.mjs` → `otp-segment-input-logic`. **Full scope:** [p6/appendices/OTP-SCOPE-P6.md](p6/appendices/OTP-SCOPE-P6.md).

Profile step (new user only):

- `display_name` required
- `email` optional on `register-complete`
- Denali tour intake does **not** collect email at UI; optional `contact.email` on upstream POST when provided (Urban requires email at intake via SDK capabilities)

---

## 5. Three apps · one tenant

Authority: [p6-host-addressing-architecture.mdoc](p6-host-addressing-architecture.mdoc)

| App | Dev (canonical) | Legacy smoke | Bootstrap |
| --- | --------------- | ------------ | --------- |
| Marketing | `{club}.localhost:3002` | `shop.{club}.localhost:3002` | `resolveMarketingBootstrapForHost` |
| Portal | `{club}.portal.localhost:3003` | `{club}.localhost:3003` | `resolvePortalBootstrapForHost` |
| Admin | `{club}.admin.localhost:3000` | `{club}.localhost:3000` | `resolveBootstrapAppSessionForHost` |

Prod platform: `{club}.{root}` · `{club}.portal.{root}` · `{club}.admin.{root}`.

Custom apex per tenant: `denali.club` · `portal.denali.club` · `admin.denali.club` (see `tenant_domains`).

All surfaces must resolve **same `tenantId`** for one club (P6-0).

